        "tekst": "[[Socialisation]] results in a **[[personal biography|Personal biography]]**: a person’s unique history of thinking, feeling and acting. You build it by interacting with others throughout your life; as the biography develops you participate in a culture while remaining in some respects a distinct individual. Without social experience, as Anna’s case shows, a biography can hardly start to emerge.\n\nSocial experience is as vital for society as for individuals. Societies outlast any person, so each generation must teach something of its way of life to the next. Broadly, socialisation is the ongoing process of **[[cultural transmission|Cultural transmission]]**.\n\nTwo theories stand out: Freud’s and Mead’s."
